    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d344">

                <pb facs="0463" n="357" xml:id="pg357"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-12-24"><hi rendition="#italic">December 24, 1890</hi>.</date>
                        (Received February 20, 1891.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1218.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith a copy
                    of the protocol on the audience question, signed the 15th ultimo by the foreign
                    representatives. As the proceedings taken here now will establish a precedent
                    for all future action, I deem it wise to follow the example of Mr. Low, set in
                    1873, and to send to you faithful copies of all the procedures taken either by
                    the yamén or the ministers.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Denby</hi>.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d344-a1.xml" xpointer="d344-a1"/>
